WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Hi kids! Welcome to Mr. Book and me stories, where stories and creativity come alive.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:17.000
Today we're visiting Forest Care Hospital, where every animal is treated with care and kindness.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:26.000
And this is the story of how one playful monkey became a true hero of the harsh.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:33.000
Nestled in the middle of green leaf forest, there stood a tall, bright building.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:42.000
This was Forest Care Hospital, where animals from all across the land came to get better and be taken care of.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:52.000
I'm Tina, I may be slow, but I never miss a corner when I'm mop. Every floor shines with love.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:59.000
I'm Cassie, I fold blankets just right and fluff every pillow. Comfort is my superpower.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:12.000
Bruno here, big boxes, water bottles or food. You name it, I carry it. Strong paws, happy heart.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:21.000
I'm Ziggy, your speedy ride. I zoom through the forest faster than the wind whenever there's an emergency.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:30.000
Hey there, I'm Puppy, I mix medicines, scribble notes and make sure everyone takes their syrup with a smiley sticker of course.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:38.000
The one who watched over everyone was Dr. Owl, a wise and kind doctor.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:47.000
Good morning team, let's care with courage and heal with heart. Remember, even the smallest job makes a big difference.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:55.000
Not far from the hospital, in the tallest mango tree of green leaf forest lived Milo the Monkey.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:03.000
Milo was famous for three things, being funny, playing pranks and never helping anyone.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:11.000
Each day the hospital staff would look up and see Milo swinging from tree to tree, singing his favorite song.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:17.000
One day Dr. Owl had asked everyone to finish their tasks early.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:23.000
Tina the tortoise squinted up at Milo's tree and called out.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:27.000
Milo, could you help me carry the mop bucket today?

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:33.000
No can do Tina, if I carry that, I might mop up my own shadow.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:37.000
Oh okay, I guess I'll carry it myself.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:42.000
Careful Tina, don't mop up any turtles by mistake.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:50.000
A few minutes later Cassie the cat came by with a big stack of freshly washed towels.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:56.000
Milo, could you fold some of these with me? It'll go faster.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:05.000
Fold towels? I only fold banana peels. Besides, towels don't taste as good.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:08.000
It's not fun doing it alone.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:17.000
Then came Bruno the bear, huffing and puffing as he dragged a cart full of supply boxes.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:26.000
Hey Milo, wanna help carry these new boxes? They're really heavy and my paws are tired.

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:33.000
Bruno, I can't risk straining my monkey muscles. They're reserved for more important things, like...

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:35.000
Tree top twirling.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:41.000
Huh, right, guess some muscles are just for showing off.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:48.000
Finally, puppy the dog came bouncing. He was carrying a tray of medicine bottles.

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:52.000
Milo, come help me count the medicine bottles.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:04:00.000
I only count coconuts, not capsules. But hey, I'll cheer you on. Go puppy go!

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:06.000
He's funny, but sometimes I wish he'd try. Just once.

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:14.000
That afternoon Milo had just invented a brand new trick called the Banana Flip Tree Leap.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:22.000
Ladies and gentle animals, prepare your paws and claws. The amazing Milo is about to fly.

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:26.000
Milo, please be careful up there.

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:30.000
Careful, I'm a professional jungle acrobat.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:34.000
He leaped from one branch to another. But...

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:38.000
Snap! The branch cracked. Slip!

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:42.000
Oh no, no no. Ah!

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:47.000
Thump! He crashed onto the ground with a painful yell.

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:54.000
Ow, ow, ow. My leg. Help! Help me! I can't move.

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:56.000
Ziggy, get the ambulance.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:03.000
Just moments later, Ziggy the zebra came galloping over in the hospital ambulance car.

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:12.000
His siren howling like a jungle owl. They carefully lifted Milo onto the soft stretcher.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:21.000
When they arrived at Forest Care Hospital, Dr. Owl was already waiting with his clipboard and warm eyes.

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:24.000
Let's take a look, my dear monkey.

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:33.000
Hmm, just a cracked leg. A bit of rest, a dash of medicine and a spoonful of kindness should do the trick.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:41.000
He wrapped Milo's leg in soft bandages and gave him a banana flavored syrup.

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:46.000
I... I didn't think anyone would come for me.

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:50.000
Of course we did. Helping heels, remember?

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:59.000
The next few days, Milo just lay in the hospital bed by the window. His leg wrapped in a soft bandage.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:04.000
Milo began to watch as the hospital team was hard at work.

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:09.000
I'll mop this hallway one more time. It has to be perfect.

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:17.000
I just want every little patient to feel warm, safe and loved.

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:24.000
These boxes are heavy, but if I carry them, someone else won't have to struggle.

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:33.000
They do so much, and I've never helped once. I just laughed. Why did they still help me?

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:39.000
Knock, knock! Hopi came in, balancing a tray with Milo's medicine.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:43.000
Time for your banana flavored syrup.

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:50.000
Just then, Cassie peaked in with a soft blanket.

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:57.000
I brought you an extra soft one. This one smells like sunshine.

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:05.000
I'm sorry. For all those times I said no, you're all still being so nice to me.

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:09.000
Two weeks later, the bandages came off.

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:16.000
Dr. Owl gently unwrapped Milo's leg, checking every little toe and bone with care.

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:22.000
I'll heal my dear Milo, strong as a coconut.

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:26.000
Thanks, Dr., for fixing me up, outside and inside.

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:33.000
The next morning, Milo didn't swing back to his mango tree instead to the laundry room.

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:40.000
Cassie was struggling with a high stack of towels. Suddenly, whoosh!

00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:47.000
Oh no, towel on my head. Captain Monkey to the rescue.

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:53.000
Banana peels are fun, but so is folding warm towels with friends.

00:07:54.000 --> 00:08:00.000
Then he saw Tina. The tortoise was slowly pushing her mop bucket.

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:05.000
Suddenly, she felt someone take the handle from her gently.

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:10.000
Reporting for sparkle duty, let's mop like the wind.

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:17.000
Thank you, Milo. Mopings not fast, but it's peaceful when you have company.

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:21.000
Next, he saw Bruno were huffing and puffing.

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:25.000
Milo rushed up and grabbed a smaller one.

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:33.000
Let's make you three, Bruno. Team power. Monkey dancing and box carrying. I'm a double threat.

00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:39.000
By the end of the day, everyone was smiling at forest care hospital.

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:47.000
You've learned well, my boy. Helping doesn't just heal wounds. It heals hearts.

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:56.000
You fixed my leg and you forgave my foolishness. Who says monkeys can't multitask?

00:08:57.000 --> 00:09:04.000
They all burst into laughter and the hospital echoed with joy and pride. Moral.

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:13.000
It's easy to joke, but it's powerful to care. Helping others brings joy to everyone.

00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:18.000
If you enjoyed the story, give us a big thumbs up, share it with your friends,

00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:24.000
and don't forget to hit the subscribe button for more magical stories.

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:27.000
See you next time.
